# Environment and stage config

`.env` (gitignored) holds only `STAGE`, `AWS_PROFILE`, `AWS_ACCOUNT_ID`, and `AWS_REGION`. `STAGE` is `dev` or `prod`.

`infra/config/config.<stage>.yml` holds stage behavior: names, feature flags, languages, profiles, runtime limits. The account and the region come from `.env` only. Synth fails when `AWS_ACCOUNT_ID` or `AWS_REGION` is missing.

Bucket names are not config and are not environment variables. `resourceName()` builds them.

The runtime slice of the YAML is the `CONFIG` environment variable on every function. Change the YAML and deploy again to change a profile.
